  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 2704.01 Specifications for Emergency Lights",
  "priorExpiration": "2004-01-26",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2704.01 Specifications for Emergency Lights.\n\n(a) Emergency lights used by hospital emergency personnel on their private vehicles shall be red in color with rotating or flashing beacon.\n\n(b) Emergency lights on a private vehicle shall be mounted as follows:\n\n(1) On the roof;\n\n(2) On the front and the rear of a vehicle if single feed lights, and not less than 12 inches from the road surface;\n\n(3) On the rear window ledges of a vehicle if rear facing lights, if they do not obstruct the driver's view to the rear or cause night time interior reflection that interferes with the driver's night time vision; or\n\n(4) On the dashboard, if they do not obstruct the driver's view or cause night time interior reflection that interferes with the driver's night time vision.\n\n(c) Emergency lights on a private vehicle shall be capable of emitting a beacon:\n\n(1) At a minimum, directly ahead and directly to the rear of the vehicle; and\n\n(2) Bright enough to be seen during normal daylight hours.\n\nSource. #4976, eff 11-14-90; ss and moved by #6174, eff 1-26-96 (from Saf-C 2702), EXPIRED: 1-26-04\n\nNew. #8073, eff 4-23-04; ss by #10084, eff 1-31-1; ss by #13214-A, eff 6-16-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2700.html"
